  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Michigan has received $6.7B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The federal government made 176,600 awards in the state, with an average award size of $38.1K, and obligations are up 1.8% year over year. The Department of Defense led buying in Michigan, obligating $3.4B, followed by the General Services Administration with $2B. Automobile Manufacturing and Military Armored Vehicle, Tank, and Tank Component Manufacturing account for the largest industry totals at $1.9B and $1.8B respectively. GENERAL DYNAMICS LAND SYSTEMS INC. is the top vendor with $1.7B, followed by FORD MOTOR CO at $756M and GENERAL MOTORS LLC at $649M. Historical annual obligations show peaks and troughs: FY22 reached $9B, then totals declined to $6.6B in FY25 before rising to $6.7B in FY26. The data are contract obligations and current-year totals are partial, covering fiscal year to date only.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How have Michigan contract obligations moved year over year?",
        "body": "Obligations are up 1.8% year over year in FY2026 to date. Obligations fell from $9B in FY22 to $6.6B in FY25, then rose to $6.7B in FY26. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer with $3.4B, which is a major share of the current total."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies, industries, and vendors dominate Michigan federal contracting?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense and the General Services Administration are the top buyers with $3.4B and $2B respectively. Automobile Manufacturing and Military Armored Vehicle, Tank, and Tank Component Manufacturing lead industries with $1.9B and $1.8B respectively. GENERAL DYNAMICS LAND SYSTEMS INC., FORD MOTOR CO, and GENERAL MOTORS LLC are the top vendors with $1.7B, $756M, and $649M respectively."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much federal contract money goes to Michigan?",
      "a": "Michigan receives $6.7B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The federal government made 176,600 awards in the state with an average award size of $38.1K. Historical annual totals include $6.8B in FY21, $9B in FY22, $8.4B in FY23, $8B in FY24, and $6.6B in FY25."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies award the most contracts in Michigan?",
      "a": "The Department of Defense awards the most contracts in Michigan, obligating $3.4B in FY2026 to date. The General Services Administration is the second-largest buyer at $2B, followed by the Department of Homeland Security at $301M and the Department of Veterans Affairs at $294M."
    },
